Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; this port may only touch riseproject-dev/python-wheels]

The _detect_machine_architecture extension (march.pybind.cc) only dummies out
cpuid() for macOS arm64, aarch64 and PowerPC; every other non-Windows target
falls into the GCC branch, which includes the x86-only <cpuid.h> and calls
__cpuid_count. On riscv64 that header does not exist, so the extension (and
therefore the whole stim wheel) fails to compile. Add __riscv to the dummied-out
list: detect_march() then returns "polyfill" and stim/__init__.py imports the
portable _stim_polyfill module, exactly as it already does on arm64. setup.py
only builds _stim_polyfill (not _stim_sse2) on non-x86, so nothing else changes.
--- a/src/stim/py/march.pybind.cc
+++ b/src/stim/py/march.pybind.cc
@@ -6,8 +6,8 @@
 //  Windows
 #include <intrin.h>
 #define cpuid(info, x) __cpuidex(info, x, 0)
-#elif (defined(__arm64__) && defined(__APPLE__)) || defined(__aarch64__) || defined(_ARCH_PPC)
-// macOS ARM64 and IBM PowerPC (dummied out)
+#elif (defined(__arm64__) && defined(__APPLE__)) || defined(__aarch64__) || defined(_ARCH_PPC) || defined(__riscv)
+// macOS ARM64, IBM PowerPC and RISC-V (dummied out)
 void cpuid(int info[4], int infoType) {
     info[0] = 0;
     info[1] = 0;
